    "site_desc": "The flux site is located on the rooftop of the Williams Science Center at Chicago State University, Chicago, Illinois. The surroundings include low-rise buildings, parking lots, trees, grassy lawns, and pedestrian pathways. The campus is bordered mainly by low-density residential neighborhoods with tree cover, while open commercial and industrial zones lie to the south and southeast. Major highways (I-94 and I-57) and rail lines are situated less than 1 km to the southwest and southeast.",
